{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"30e8e41e5ab44c4e1c92faebc0aa2a6ead56ffc0a63dbf3043d95b85ca2a94ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI workflows (module-size gate)","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/module-size-allowlist.txt","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reconcile.py"],"problem_keywords":["module-size gate","allowlist drain","ci shell","grep exit code","pipefail","set -e"],"propositions":["The module-size gate shell step aborts with exit 1 when the allowlist is empty or comment-only because grep returns 1 on no match, triggering pipefail+set -e.","Wrapping the grep command with '|| true' prevents the no-match exit code from aborting the step while preserving correct behavior for non-empty allowlists.","The same guard must be applied to the identical 'listed=' line in both gerrit-verify.yaml and test.yml before the allowlist-emptying reconcile change can land.","The gate must continue to fail (exit 1) when a non-allow-listed file exceeds the 800 LOC ceiling, ensuring over-cap detection is not broken."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787906251769100001,"uuid":"1ee8f27a-db24-4d35-8d77-d59a65fa453a"}